Task 1: Set up monitoring for VM metrics using Prometheus and Grafana
Subtask 1.1: Verify Monitoring Stack Installation
First, let's verify that the monitoring components are properly installed and running.

Check the monitoring namespace and pods:
oc get pods -n openshift-monitoring
Verify Prometheus is running:
oc get prometheus -n openshift-monitoring
Check Grafana deployment:
oc get deployment grafana -n openshift-monitoring
List available ServiceMonitors:
oc get servicemonitor -n openshift-monitoring
Subtask 1.2: Enable VM Metrics Collection
Create a ServiceMonitor for VM metrics:
cat << EOF | oc apply -f -
apiVersion: monitoring.coreos.com/v1
kind: ServiceMonitor
metadata:
  name: vm-metrics-monitor
  namespace: openshift-monitoring
  labels:
    app: vm-monitoring
spec:
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      kubevirt.io: virt-launcher
  endpoints:
  - port: metrics
    interval: 30s
    path: /metrics
EOF
Verify the ServiceMonitor was created:
oc get servicemonitor vm-metrics-monitor -n openshift-monitoring
Subtask 1.3: Create a Test Virtual Machine for Monitoring
Create a sample VM with monitoring labels:
cat << EOF | oc apply -f -
apiVersion: kubevirt.io/v1
kind: VirtualMachine
metadata:
  name: monitoring-test-vm
  namespace: default
  labels:
    app: test-vm
    monitoring: enabled
spec:
  running: true
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        kubevirt.io/vm: monitoring-test-vm
        app: test-vm
    spec:
      domain:
        cpu:
          cores: 1
        memory:
          guest: 1Gi
        devices:
          disks:
          - name: containerdisk
            disk:
              bus: virtio
          - name: cloudinitdisk
            disk:
              bus: virtio
          interfaces:
          - name: default
            masquerade: {}
        resources:
          requests:
            memory: 1Gi
            cpu: 100m
          limits:
            memory: 1Gi
            cpu: 500m
      networks:
      - name: default
        pod: {}
      volumes:
      - name: containerdisk
        containerDisk:
          image: quay.io/kubevirt/cirros-container-disk-demo
      - name: cloudinitdisk
        cloudInitNoCloud:
          userDataBase64: SGkuXG4=
EOF
